# SUPPLIED stimulus for whole minion_tlb (B11), from the PINNED CORE-ET DV
# sequence -- hw/ip/minion/tlb/dv/minion_tlb_test.cc fill_entry (136-184), its
# first call at :299.  Generated mechanically; values decode back to the
# audited hex.
#
#   req_data_i      (ord  7, w48) = 0x580000001110
#   ptw_resp_data_i (ord  5, w64) = 0x2af378c7
#   satp_info_i     (ord 11, w32) = 0x80010000
#
# THE PINNED ORDER, one source tick per two sub-steps.  `SimCtrl::tick()` in
# dv/common/sim_ctrl.h drives clk_i LOW, evaluates, then HIGH, evaluates -- so
# the even sub-step is the low half and the odd one the high half, and clk_i is
# driven EXPLICITLY here because the emitted flop 0 enable is
# (clk_i == 0 AND phase == 0) and the memory commits at phase 0.
#
#   ticks 0-1  reset: rst_ni low
#   tick  2    set_split_req: req_valid high, request presented; ready LOW
#   tick  3    ptw_req_valid_o expected; ready still LOW
#   tick  4    ptw_req_ready_i HIGH for exactly one tick -- the ack
#   tick  5    ready LOW again, PTW leaf response presented, resp_valid HIGH
#   tick  6    resp_valid HELD -- the documented two-tick hold, because
#              rf_latch_wr_en reads ptw_resp_valid_q, not _i
#   tick  7    clear_ptw_resp: response and valid cleared
#   tick  8    quiet tail, for disabled/quiet preservation
#
# An earlier version held ready constantly high, dropped req_valid after
# sub-step 3, omitted clk_i and ended with the response still asserted.  It is
# retained as a preflight negative.
stim v1
in 12 1 0
in 1 1 0
in 13 2 0
in 8 1 0
in 3 32 0
in 11 32 2147549184
in 7 48 96757023248656
at 0 in 0 1 0
at 0 in 10 1 0
at 0 in 9 1 0
